<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Cementation half year share dips.</title>
<headline>Cementation half year share dips.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended March 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, (cts)		25.7	  vs 35.9</p>
<p>    Net asset value shr (cts) 843.6   vs 783.7</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 nil	   vs 12.5</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   2.29	  vs 3.21</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   4.43	  vs 5.59</p>
<p>    Tax			 2.12	  vs 2.38</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   3.34	  vs 1.55</p>
<p>    Turnover		  270.23	vs 257.54</p>
<p>Full name: Cementation Co Africa Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The firm said the drop in attributable earnings was mostly because of a rise in its interest charge which was related to an increase in borrowings.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
